{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778978834148,"sessionID":"ses_1cc99dc71ffejo0BR3P2x1kan5","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"call_Uyp8vWafmoaMjpgYFGGu8lzx","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"term_tracker_item.*3506|3506","path":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/src/ontology","include":"cl-edit.owl"},"output":"Found 4 matches\n/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/src/ontology/cl-edit.owl:\n  Line 8445: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000550 \"FMA:83506\")\n\n  Line 24993: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:NV\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20807514\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21828096\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26053743\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34128468\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35067985\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0011111 \"a specialized neuroendocrine cell that synthesizes and secretes GnRH decapeptide, a key regulator of reproductive function. It originates from the olfactory placode during embryonic development and migrates into the forebrain where it localises predominantly in the hypothalamus and in humans, in extrahypothalamic regions like the basal ganglia (Skrapits et al., 2021). This cell regulates reproduction by secreting GnRH into the pituitary portal vessels to induce the release of gonadotropins into the general circulation. It expresses receptor subunits required for AMPA, NMDA, and kainate receptor signaling and may use glutamate as a neurotransmitter in recurrent collateral innervation.\")\n\n  Line 25538: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31857493\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35069694\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020013 \"A fibroblast forming the connective tissue sheath that encloses the hair follicle epithelium from the level of the bulge downward to the hair bulb. This cell expresses characteristic markers, including DPEP1 in humans and COL11A1 and ACTA2 (alpha-smooth muscle actin) in mice and humans. Dermal sheath fibroblast possesses contractile properties mediated by calcium-calmodulin-myosin light chain kinase signalling, generating centripetal force during hair follicle catagen that relocates the dermal papilla to the stem cell niche.\")\n\n  Line 35327: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25465495\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29691589\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35036581\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35069694\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4072103 \"A bipotent mesenchymal stem cell that resides in the dermal sheath, specifically within the dermal sheath cup at the base of the hair follicle, characterized by its capacity for self-renewal and differentiation into both dermal sheath and dermal papilla cells throughout hair cycling. In humans, this cell is marked by enriched expression of gremlin-2 (GREM2) and dipeptidase-1 (DPEP1), and acts as a progenitor reservoir sustaining and regenerating the follicle's mesenchymal compartments.\")\n","metadata":{"matches":4,"truncated":false},"title":"term_tracker_item.*3506|3506","time":{"start":1778978834102,"end":1778978834146}},"id":"prt_e3366c6b1001Iobheysrawf29B","sessionID":"ses_1cc99dc71ffejo0BR3P2x1kan5","messageID":"msg_e3366a02a001lzkRfur8LPwwuX"}}
